WEBVTT

00:05.990 --> 00:07.290
I don't understand.

00:09.160 --> 00:13.950
This is the purpose for which 
humans created my vessel.

00:14.720 --> 00:17.500
To make other humans suffer...

00:18.000 --> 00:22.790
This is the cruelty that humans 
wrought into me at birth.

00:24.060 --> 00:28.170
I was merely doing what they 
made me for... and yet...

00:28.170 --> 00:30.650
Why am I treated this way? 
I do not understand.

00:32.640 --> 00:35.720
I was merely being what I am,

00:36.030 --> 00:37.660
Kadomori Taiju.

00:38.630 --> 00:41.520
Tsukumogami such as yourselves 
would normally be

00:41.520 --> 00:44.280
declared unfit for life 
in the land of the living.

00:44.280 --> 00:48.730
Your marebito would be stripped out 
and returned to the land of the dead.

00:48.730 --> 00:50.100
"Unfit"?

00:50.680 --> 00:55.210
So hung up on your vessel, 
you refuse to live your own life.

00:55.210 --> 00:57.490
Wouldn't you rather just be an object?

00:57.490 --> 00:58.990
No. I—

00:58.990 --> 01:03.560
No deeper thoughts, 
just switched on at all times.

01:05.320 --> 01:07.560
Still, I used you.

01:08.040 --> 01:10.550
I thought you might just be useful.

01:11.460 --> 01:15.530
But then you went and turned on me.

01:19.110 --> 01:21.960
You're worthless scrap.

01:22.360 --> 01:24.380
Don't understand why you're treated this way?

01:25.240 --> 01:27.060
Better learn, then.

01:28.800 --> 01:31.400
Scrap's got to be disposed of.

01:38.130 --> 01:43.190
I'll tell the men that we had our revenge.

01:54.880 --> 02:02.640
<i>Malevolent Spirits</i>

03:15.960 --> 03:20.970
<b>Radiance</b>

03:27.480 --> 03:30.120
Papa says he finished the job.

03:30.720 --> 03:32.230
Mission complete, right?

03:32.560 --> 03:33.640
I'm finished.

03:33.640 --> 03:34.650
Thank you.

03:34.650 --> 03:36.700
Did you hurt your leg bad, Hyoma-chan?

03:36.700 --> 03:38.160
No, it's no issue.

03:38.160 --> 03:39.610
Pants on fire.

03:40.520 --> 03:43.860
Tsubaki, you're pursuing 
the paper umbrella, as well?

03:43.860 --> 03:46.170
Sure am. You heard?

03:46.590 --> 03:49.980
You mentioned my siblings' names before.

03:49.980 --> 03:52.870
Is your quest related to their deaths?

03:54.400 --> 03:59.560
We had a few get-togethers 
for group training.

04:00.110 --> 04:01.380
Information brokers...

04:01.380 --> 04:04.390
They were really strong, 
and they were nice to me.

04:06.500 --> 04:09.960
Watching them in action... 
It was like poetry.

04:14.630 --> 04:17.180
The specialty training of the Kyoto Saenome,

04:17.180 --> 04:18.700
Ten Vessels Sparring.

04:19.150 --> 04:21.900
They mastered it so quickly.

04:21.900 --> 04:23.450
Impressive indeed.

04:24.280 --> 04:26.440
Watch close, Tsubaki.

04:26.440 --> 04:30.200
They're what we call prodigies, just like you.

04:31.360 --> 04:36.410
I'd never met anyone who made 
my heart sing like they did.

04:38.740 --> 04:43.260
Things were so much fun when 
Kusui-san and Hayato-san were around.

04:43.960 --> 04:47.260
I'm pursuing the paper umbrella 
because it stole them from me.

04:47.990 --> 04:52.340
It's the first tsukumogami I feel 
determined to beat with my own hands.

04:54.210 --> 04:57.900
If you feel the same way, 
maybe we could work together?

04:58.910 --> 05:02.080
The Kyoto Saenome have an 
unparalleled information network.

05:02.080 --> 05:05.930
And it's the most likely place to run into 
newly manifested tsukumogami.

05:07.780 --> 05:12.040
So instead of staying shut up in the 
Nagatsuki household, you should join me,

05:12.040 --> 05:13.270
Hyoma-chan.

05:16.860 --> 05:21.480
<i>I'm sure you'll find it 
an appealing invitation.</i>

05:21.480 --> 05:25.210
<i>But it's dangerous to take that hand.</i>

05:25.210 --> 05:27.960
<i>Kadomori Tsubaki was only 
eight years old when she mastered</i>

05:27.960 --> 05:30.140
<i>the Kyoto Saenome's ultimate training,</i>

05:30.140 --> 05:32.160
<i>Ten Vessels Sparring.</i>

05:32.160 --> 05:35.880
<i>And around age ten, she was 
outdoing even experienced Saenome.</i>

05:35.880 --> 05:37.720
<i>The Kadomori Prodigy...</i>

05:38.600 --> 05:40.110
That's enough, Tsubaki.

05:40.460 --> 05:43.830
I don't need you ruining all 
our workers just for practice.

05:44.980 --> 05:45.990
It's just...

05:46.790 --> 05:48.330
boring.

05:48.910 --> 05:51.320
<i>Her feelings for your siblings...</i>

05:51.320 --> 05:54.160
<i>and even for the paper umbrella...</i>

05:54.160 --> 05:56.600
<i>differ from yours in a definitive way.</i>

05:57.160 --> 05:58.540
You think I look happy?

05:59.090 --> 06:00.130
You can tell?

06:01.120 --> 06:03.000
I found something...

06:03.970 --> 06:05.980
A wonderful toy.

06:05.980 --> 06:09.510
<i>It's all a game to entertain herself.</i>

06:10.400 --> 06:16.670
<i>And she has inherited the Kadomori 
philosophy—use whatever you can</i>

06:16.670 --> 06:18.970
<i>to achieve your goal.</i>

06:21.020 --> 06:23.740
<i>Despite that, Hyoma, will you...</i>

06:25.990 --> 06:27.030
Let me think.

06:27.890 --> 06:29.560
"Destroy the paper umbrella."

06:30.220 --> 06:32.330
This has been my oath,

06:32.330 --> 06:37.160
and the source of the hatred that's 
consumed me for close to ten years now.

06:37.840 --> 06:39.240
We are the same.

06:39.240 --> 06:41.170
I'm pursuing it, as well.

06:41.940 --> 06:43.430
Your offer is most welcome.

06:45.880 --> 06:46.920
However,

06:46.920 --> 06:50.700
I currently have other commitments 
I can't back away from,

06:51.320 --> 06:53.430
so I fear I must courteously decline.

06:55.220 --> 06:56.010
Huh?

07:00.740 --> 07:02.840
You really did overdo it.

07:02.840 --> 07:05.820
Certainly not! I merely 
turned my heart to iron—

07:05.820 --> 07:08.650
That's what we call "overdoing it."

07:09.550 --> 07:13.070
But why were you all so surprised?

07:13.570 --> 07:16.670
Tsubaki seemed truly puzzled by my answer.

07:16.670 --> 07:18.580
Aogi and Uchiki were, too.

07:19.250 --> 07:22.330
Still, you weren't tempted at all?

07:24.360 --> 07:26.460
"I will destroy the paper umbrella myself."

07:26.990 --> 07:28.960
That is my unimpeachable goal.

07:30.020 --> 07:33.510
But that's not all I swore 
before their grave.

07:34.090 --> 07:39.480
The oath I swore was to become 
truly strong, in body and mind,

07:39.480 --> 07:42.520
so that I could stop the next 
tsukumogami-induced tragedy.

07:44.070 --> 07:48.920
I believe that my training in the Nagatsuki 
household is equally in pursuit of that goal.

07:49.810 --> 07:52.360
And there's the matter of Botan, as well.

07:56.390 --> 07:58.040
W-Well...

07:58.680 --> 08:02.110
Is this an "I can't abandon my 
betrothed" sort of statement?

08:02.110 --> 08:04.080
That seems rather presumptuous.

08:04.080 --> 08:05.200
You lecher!

08:05.200 --> 08:07.740
No! It's merely the circumstances in which she—

08:07.740 --> 08:08.640
L-Lecher?!

08:08.640 --> 08:12.670
Men are such pigs!

08:13.040 --> 08:14.040
Have I...

08:15.520 --> 08:17.540
Is that the impression I give?

08:18.000 --> 08:19.930
Of an unlikely lecher?

08:22.360 --> 08:23.640
Idiot.

08:25.170 --> 08:26.630
You stupid idiot!

08:27.690 --> 08:30.090
You came back <i>so</i> injured!

08:30.850 --> 08:32.260
I'm sorry.

08:34.530 --> 08:35.950
Hyoma-san!

08:36.400 --> 08:37.520
Find it?

08:37.520 --> 08:40.480
No. Nothing there either?

08:40.480 --> 08:42.450
I just can't figure out where 
it could've gotten put.

08:42.450 --> 08:45.150
What's Kushige up to, anyway?

08:45.150 --> 08:47.140
Playing shogi with a guy from 
the neighborhood association.

08:47.940 --> 08:49.550
They do it all the time.

08:49.550 --> 08:52.340
Tsukumogami can be conscientious neighbors?

08:52.340 --> 08:58.350
White Team  Red Team

08:52.340 --> 08:58.350
White Team  Red Team

08:52.680 --> 08:55.860
Nagi even took part in the parents' 
relay on sports day and stuff.

08:56.250 --> 08:57.850
What in the world?

08:58.720 --> 09:01.540
Tsukumogami are quite varied, it seems.

09:04.240 --> 09:04.860
What is it?

09:04.860 --> 09:06.860
Oh, nothing!

09:06.860 --> 09:08.360
You go down the stairs first.

09:13.640 --> 09:16.810
<i>What a mess. I hate you, Haori!</i>

09:17.320 --> 09:18.120
Listen, all.

09:18.790 --> 09:21.690
Botan will be starting 
her third year in university,

09:21.690 --> 09:25.350
and Hyoma-san will be starting 
his third month with us.

09:25.870 --> 09:28.880
To celebrate the occasion, tonight...

09:29.360 --> 09:30.750
We're having hot pot!

09:30.750 --> 09:33.630
Heck yes!

09:34.310 --> 09:35.930
Hot pot?

09:35.930 --> 09:38.490
Was that really the purpose of this meeting?

09:38.490 --> 09:41.800
Hot pot is a big event in this household.

09:41.800 --> 09:44.270
We only have it during celebrations like this,

09:44.270 --> 09:46.540
so it gets everyone into a festive mood.

09:47.940 --> 09:49.300
Even Botan?

09:50.600 --> 09:54.030
Now I'm going to assign roles for shopping.

09:54.030 --> 09:55.100
Yes, ma'am!

09:55.100 --> 09:56.520
I'll buy the meat.

09:56.520 --> 09:57.960
Yu will buy the other ingredients.

09:57.960 --> 09:58.720
Yes, ma'am!

09:58.720 --> 10:02.330
Eggs, sides, that kind of thing: Suzuri, Kagami.

10:02.330 --> 10:02.920
Right-o!

10:02.920 --> 10:03.710
You got it!

10:03.710 --> 10:05.360
Nagi's on alcohol duty.

10:05.360 --> 10:06.080
Heck yeah!

10:06.080 --> 10:09.540
Kushige, stay in the mansion 
in case of trouble.

10:09.900 --> 10:11.530
What about Hyoma-san and me?

10:11.530 --> 10:15.530
You find the big self-heating pot 
we stashed away somewhere.

10:16.020 --> 10:17.880
Go for it, Hyoma!

10:17.880 --> 10:21.130
We all gotta chip in to 
make the hot pot happen!

10:19.570 --> 10:20.250
What?

10:20.250 --> 10:23.080
Botan, it'll be just you and Hyoma-san.

10:21.130 --> 10:23.800
You seem very serious about hot pot.

10:23.080 --> 10:24.100
Make the best of it.

10:23.800 --> 10:28.040
C'mon, man! Get a clue!

10:24.850 --> 10:25.680
What?

10:25.680 --> 10:28.620
He's in the running to be your 
future husband, remember?

10:28.040 --> 10:31.920
You gotta learn the truth 
of what hot pot's all about.

10:28.620 --> 10:30.700
I want you moving things along.

10:30.700 --> 10:33.610
I-I never signed up for that!

10:31.920 --> 10:34.460
You'll see, man.

10:33.130 --> 10:34.460
What are you talking about?

10:33.610 --> 10:36.440
And Hyoma-san doesn't seem interested...

10:35.550 --> 10:37.550
Is it really that important?

10:36.440 --> 10:39.880
If you don't make your move, 
he never will be!

10:39.880 --> 10:42.140
Surely you fancy him at least 
a <i>little</i> bit, don't you?

10:42.140 --> 10:44.860
I-I do believe he's a good person,

10:44.860 --> 10:47.360
but that doesn't mean 
I have special... well...

10:47.360 --> 10:49.290
I just don't look at him that way!

10:49.290 --> 10:50.670
Someone's blushing!

10:50.670 --> 10:51.980
We're not children!

10:52.830 --> 10:54.640
A cheat sheet of questions.

10:52.830 --> 10:58.340
<b>Step 2              Investigate his likes and interests</b>

10:52.830 --> 10:58.840
<b>Steps for Love</b>

10:52.830 --> 10:58.840
<b>~ Hyoma Version ~</b>

10:52.830 --> 10:58.840
<b>By Haori</b>

10:52.830 --> 10:58.840
<b>Step 1               Investigate his past romantic history</b>

10:54.640 --> 10:57.700
While you look for the pot, 
try and feel him out.

10:58.840 --> 11:02.740
<i>Honestly... She's made me all self-conscious!</i>

11:03.350 --> 11:04.080
Botan.

11:04.470 --> 11:05.920
Y-Yes?!

11:05.920 --> 11:09.790
A pot for this many people 
would be quite large, correct?

11:09.790 --> 11:12.920
Is there any chance you stored it 
in the outside warehouse?

11:12.920 --> 11:14.730
Oh... It might be there.

11:14.730 --> 11:16.610
All right. I'll search there.

11:16.610 --> 11:21.480
<i>He doesn't seem like the kind of person 
to have a romantic history...</i>

11:23.620 --> 11:24.740
<b>Beef Heaven</b>

11:24.740 --> 11:25.870
<b>Today's Special
Domestic Black Wagyu Beef
Half Price!!</b>

11:24.740 --> 11:25.870
<b>Today's Special
Domestic Black Wagyu Beef
Half Price!!</b>

11:27.870 --> 11:29.750
<b>Beef Corner</b>

11:38.410 --> 11:39.590
Excellent.

11:40.040 --> 11:41.450
Mission complete!

11:42.080 --> 11:43.770
Now to go home and enjoy a cup of tea.

11:45.320 --> 11:49.370
<i>But after getting them some alone time, 
I probably shouldn't hurry back...</i>

11:51.960 --> 11:54.020
<i>I'll grab my tea out.</i>

12:00.100 --> 12:01.440
Oh, drat!

12:01.440 --> 12:03.990
I left them home alone together.

12:04.870 --> 12:08.490
Blinded by the promise of hot pot, 
I have made a grievous error.

12:08.490 --> 12:11.870
<b>Fried Tofu</b>

12:09.220 --> 12:11.430
I need free hands.

12:19.060 --> 12:20.630
I'll return soon.

12:21.760 --> 12:22.730
Botan...

12:23.780 --> 12:25.260
Shoyokyo!

12:27.830 --> 12:31.160
That mackerel, the amberjack on the right, 
the sea bream in the back, and these oysters!

12:31.790 --> 12:32.890
I'll take them!

12:32.890 --> 12:34.090
Excellent eye!

12:34.090 --> 12:36.400
She picked all the best of the catch!

12:36.760 --> 12:39.220
These strawberries are 
charming and appetizing...

12:41.140 --> 12:43.280
Just like you, young miss.

12:43.280 --> 12:56.540
Green
Grocer
Noriki

12:43.710 --> 12:44.520
Oh, you!

12:44.520 --> 12:49.070
You've sold me, then. I'll take one more box.

12:49.070 --> 12:52.360
In exchange, dear... 
do you think you might...

12:52.360 --> 12:54.590
What a smooth talker!

12:54.590 --> 12:56.540
I'll let you have it all at half price!

12:57.250 --> 12:59.290
What a haul!

12:59.290 --> 13:01.610
What else were we gonna buy again?

13:02.690 --> 13:04.560
Why not grab some cake while we're out?

13:04.560 --> 13:06.050
Great idea!

13:07.620 --> 13:08.430
Hey.

13:08.930 --> 13:10.680
The Kadomoris gave me the lowdown.

13:11.510 --> 13:14.760
A special exception, 
assigned the task of making sake...

13:15.610 --> 13:17.400
The koji box tsukumogami!

13:18.200 --> 13:19.910
A Nagatsuki, eh?

13:20.350 --> 13:22.820
Didn't expect you to darken my door.

13:23.540 --> 13:27.570
I'm here for a bit of your legendary sake.

13:28.310 --> 13:30.460
I won't be unfair.

13:31.080 --> 13:34.580
Defeat me in a competition, 
and you can have it.

13:34.580 --> 13:35.580
Sounds great.

13:36.470 --> 13:38.960
Glad we could get right down to business.

13:40.930 --> 13:44.330
It seems you don't know the 
nature of this competition.

13:44.780 --> 13:48.340
Very well. I'll show you.

13:50.880 --> 13:52.310
It's this.

13:52.730 --> 13:54.200
Fine by me!

13:54.200 --> 13:54.810
Let's...

13:55.350 --> 13:56.430
Fight!

14:07.860 --> 14:11.030
<i>What the heck's wrong with me?</i>

14:16.060 --> 14:18.330
Let's see...

14:22.200 --> 14:25.940
<i>He's fine, and I'm all flustered. 
It's a little disheartening.</i>

14:26.510 --> 14:30.520
<i>I mean, why am I the only one thinking 
about the trial arranged marriage?</i>

14:30.970 --> 14:34.200
<i>Shouldn't it be on Hyoma-san's mind, too?</i>

14:34.200 --> 14:37.580
<i>If I'm the only one... bothered about it...</i>

14:37.960 --> 14:38.850
<i>Well, it's not fair!</i>

14:40.070 --> 14:44.390
<i>Although... maybe Hyoma-san's 
really not like that.</i>

14:44.390 --> 14:48.560
<i>If he doesn't get crushes or feel 
romantic feelings for others,</i>

14:48.560 --> 14:51.630
<i>it's possible the arranged marriage 
thing really isn't on his mind!</i>

14:49.670 --> 14:50.670
Botan?

14:51.630 --> 14:52.370
Botan?

14:53.590 --> 14:54.410
Are you all right?

14:54.410 --> 14:56.000
Wh-What?!

14:56.000 --> 14:58.490
Well... you were looking rather ill.

14:58.490 --> 15:01.500
I can take over here if you'd like to rest.

15:03.800 --> 15:06.740
<i>Whose fault is it that I feel ill?!</i>

15:07.380 --> 15:09.760
<i>Oh, right... It's Haori's.</i>

15:15.720 --> 15:18.270
That's actually a relief.

15:18.930 --> 15:23.080
Oh, nothing. I was just 
thinking about something.

15:23.080 --> 15:24.250
About what?

15:24.250 --> 15:26.360
I'm going to check the second floor.

15:27.400 --> 15:29.820
Botan, you dropped something.

15:31.540 --> 15:35.160
"Step 1: Investigate his past romantic history.

15:35.160 --> 15:36.650
Step 2..."

15:36.970 --> 15:38.010
What is this?

15:38.010 --> 15:40.540
Just some stupid thing Haori wrote!

15:40.540 --> 15:42.220
Why do you have this?

15:43.290 --> 15:45.560
About the arranged marriage, um...

15:45.560 --> 15:50.580
Haori wanted things to move forward, 
so she kind of forced it on me.

15:51.130 --> 15:52.800
I-It's not what you think?

15:53.510 --> 15:56.510
Is this what was bothering you?

15:56.510 --> 15:58.260
They're truly incorrigible.

15:59.320 --> 16:01.070
You don't need to worry about it.

16:01.070 --> 16:02.520
I'm not worried about it.

16:03.980 --> 16:06.460
<i>He's colder than I thought!</i>

16:09.600 --> 16:10.690
Hyoma-san?

16:11.040 --> 16:12.780
Are you blushing a little?

16:13.200 --> 16:15.020
I know not of what you speak.

16:15.020 --> 16:16.590
My behavior is normal.

16:16.590 --> 16:18.700
Might we venture to the second floor?

16:20.580 --> 16:22.320
Hey. Hey!

16:22.320 --> 16:24.460
Could I get a quick look at your face?

16:24.830 --> 16:28.100
My eyes have already locked on to 
the cardboard box before me.

16:28.640 --> 16:31.380
Would looking away not 
be negligence, forsooth?

16:31.740 --> 16:32.950
<i>"Forsooth"?</i>

16:33.890 --> 16:35.440
<i>Suzuri mentioned this...</i>

16:35.440 --> 16:40.440
<i>When Hyoma-kun gets flustered, 
he sometimes slips into old-timey speech.</i>

16:40.440 --> 16:42.250
<i>He says "wherefore" and such.</i>

16:53.610 --> 16:55.050
Wherefore? Wherefore?!

16:55.050 --> 16:56.270
I'm curious!

16:56.270 --> 16:57.790
<i>And</i> I want revenge!

16:57.790 --> 17:00.870
Revenge?! What are you suggesting I've done—

17:07.600 --> 17:11.380
<i>He's... bright red.</i>

17:20.790 --> 17:21.760
B-Botan?

17:21.760 --> 17:22.770
Y-Yes?!

17:24.020 --> 17:25.960
Might you remove yourself from my person?

17:27.840 --> 17:32.830
What the hell is going on here?!

17:32.830 --> 17:34.900
Kunato...

17:35.340 --> 17:39.750
Hyoma!

17:41.910 --> 17:44.410
Well, I had a wonderful time.

17:44.860 --> 17:47.830
I hope we can play again soon, Kushige-san.

17:49.350 --> 17:51.000
The evil has been purged.

17:51.000 --> 17:53.130
I don't know about evil...

17:53.130 --> 17:56.540
Did you find the large 
self-heating pot, though?

17:57.080 --> 17:58.890
Large self-heating pot?

17:58.890 --> 18:00.950
You mean the one we borrowed?

18:07.560 --> 18:08.880
That's right!

18:08.880 --> 18:12.820
I lent it to the neighborhood association 
for a festival and forgot to get it back!

18:12.820 --> 18:14.820
I'm so sorry, you two!

18:15.670 --> 18:17.840
It's no laughing matter!

18:17.840 --> 18:19.320
We're back.

18:19.320 --> 18:21.160
What happened to Nagi?

18:21.160 --> 18:23.420
We found him passed out at the front door.

18:24.590 --> 18:26.920
I had a battle...

18:27.730 --> 18:29.330
A drinking battle.

18:29.910 --> 18:32.840
It was a damn hard fight...

18:33.330 --> 18:36.460
But I won the legendary sake!

18:36.460 --> 18:38.320
One bottle might not be enough.

18:38.320 --> 18:40.780
And you only got Japanese sake? 
Where's my cocktails?

18:40.780 --> 18:41.790
And my red wine?

18:41.790 --> 18:43.020
And my whisky?!

18:43.020 --> 18:45.080
Huh? Didn't get any...

18:45.080 --> 18:47.210
Go back out and get more.

18:47.210 --> 18:48.520
No way!

18:49.270 --> 18:52.080
Well, we've more or less got what we need,

18:52.080 --> 18:53.980
so let's start getting ready!

18:53.980 --> 18:55.020
Hot pot time!

18:55.020 --> 18:57.400
Yeah!

19:01.530 --> 19:04.240
Let's eat!

19:04.660 --> 19:07.410
<b>Celebrating Botan's Third Year
And Hyoma-san's Three Months!</b>

19:07.410 --> 19:09.130
Huh? Where's the sashimi?

19:09.130 --> 19:10.420
Over here.

19:10.420 --> 19:13.260
Kushige! I'm takin' your shochu!

19:10.680 --> 19:12.730
Do you like a lot of vegetables, Yu?

19:12.730 --> 19:14.170
Yes, thank you.

19:17.000 --> 19:19.720
Hey, Nagi! Don't hog the beef!

19:18.830 --> 19:23.980
It appears that growing accustomed to human 
form gives tsukumogami a taste for food.

19:19.720 --> 19:21.840
Give me your dish! You're getting veggies!

19:21.840 --> 19:23.350
No way!

19:23.980 --> 19:25.700
They're amazing.

19:29.810 --> 19:31.740
Kagami, your Kahlua and milk.

19:31.740 --> 19:33.160
Hey, thanks!

19:33.160 --> 19:35.440
Kagami, you're too young to drink alcohol!

19:35.440 --> 19:37.690
Aw... In that case...

19:40.020 --> 19:41.600
I can do it now, right?

19:41.600 --> 19:43.530
Don't transform trivially!

19:43.530 --> 19:46.180
Hyoma! What team're you on?

19:46.180 --> 19:48.080
We're all big drinkers here.

19:48.080 --> 19:49.930
And I'm team Japanese sake!

19:49.930 --> 19:53.500
Hyoma, come join Team Kahlua and Milk!

19:53.500 --> 19:56.330
Er, I'm not particularly 
well-versed in alcoholic—

19:56.330 --> 19:57.680
That's right!

19:57.680 --> 20:00.250
You're Team Newbie like me!

20:00.250 --> 20:03.260
Let's get along, Kunato-kun...

20:00.480 --> 20:01.770
H-Hey!

20:03.260 --> 20:05.000
Botan?

20:05.730 --> 20:07.270
Are you drunk?

20:07.270 --> 20:09.420
I get it now.

20:10.600 --> 20:13.610
At the end of the day...

20:13.610 --> 20:15.840
...you're just after Botan.

20:15.840 --> 20:17.820
I-I'll bring some water to sober her up!

20:19.840 --> 20:22.120
Huh? We out of beef?

20:22.810 --> 20:24.810
I want more!

20:24.390 --> 20:25.640
Are you all right?

20:24.810 --> 20:26.320
There's more over there!

20:25.640 --> 20:27.860
Yeah, thanks.

20:34.820 --> 20:36.350
Hyoma-san...

20:36.350 --> 20:38.250
Sorry I went overboard earlier.

20:38.250 --> 20:39.680
N-No matter...

20:39.680 --> 20:42.550
It was Haori's fault for 
the silly trick she played.

20:44.290 --> 20:48.240
Are big sisters like that in every household?

20:48.240 --> 20:49.600
Big sisters?

20:49.600 --> 20:52.560
Mine made life difficult for me long ago.

20:52.840 --> 20:55.290
I was still merely a child,

20:55.290 --> 20:59.820
but she interrogated me and advised me 
about friends of the opposite sex at school.

21:01.860 --> 21:03.980
She was a formidable big sister.

21:04.850 --> 21:06.020
Oh, really?

21:09.350 --> 21:12.220
The Nagatsuki tsukumogami are quite raucous.

21:13.560 --> 21:16.460
They celebrate and converse 
with great enthusiasm,

21:16.460 --> 21:18.970
and make clear their deep affection for you.

21:19.420 --> 21:22.470
I'd never met tsukumogami like them before.

21:26.560 --> 21:28.200
You have a fine family.

21:29.750 --> 21:31.000
Thank you.

21:32.760 --> 21:35.720
Hey, asshole! I worked hard for that shit, 
and you ain't even drunk it!

21:33.900 --> 21:35.480
Stop it! Let me go!

21:35.720 --> 21:37.050
Just have some!

21:37.600 --> 21:39.450
Down it quick!

21:38.190 --> 21:40.810
Meanwhile, we'll have some girly talk!

21:39.450 --> 21:41.110
Lay off! Stop i—

21:40.810 --> 21:43.640
Anything happen while we were gone?

21:42.940 --> 21:44.180
Ah, it's good.

21:43.640 --> 21:45.360
Tell us all about it!

21:44.750 --> 21:46.540
Right?!

21:45.690 --> 21:47.210
You pushed <i>him</i> to the floor?!

21:46.540 --> 21:49.130
Now try a cocktail!

21:47.210 --> 21:49.580
A reverse floor slam!

21:49.580 --> 21:52.270
N-No! It wasn't like—

23:24.880 --> 23:39.890
<b>Next Time</b>

23:24.880 --> 23:39.890
<b>Ambush</b>
